## STEP 1 — DELTA

[NEW] **Recognized-slug redirect class on the origin** — `/tools`, `/staff`, `/rails`, `/uploads`, `/karriere` return 301 to a first-party `https://hypofriend.de/en/exchange?share_id=…&link_id=…`, *not* the canonical `https://hypofriend.de/` shell every other unknown path returns. Negative controls: `/backoffice`, `/internal`, `/sidekiq`, `/admin`, `/graphql`, `/api/v1|v2|v4`, `/webhooks`, `/uploads`-adjacent names, `/immobilien`, `/darlehnen`, `/beratung`, `/kredit`, `/rechner`, `/compare`, `/contact`, `/team`, `/jobs`, `/presse`, and random slugs (`/zzz-det-abc123`) all → canonical shell. Never mapped in 27 cycles.
[NEW] **`share_id` + `link_id` are deterministic per slug and DB-backed** — `/tools` twice returned the identical pair `share_id=dddb5cba-7e96-44b2-be7d-bb621c8a8e68`, `link_id=cb8917e2-41d9-5ae9-bf82-d3a5ecc97705`; `/staff` → `f46e3e93-…`/`0df9db96-…`; `/karriere` → `a21edcd8-…`. `link_id` is a real identifier: it resolves to a live auth-free `GET /en/account/property-search/expose-<link_id>` → **200, 3766B**.
[NEW] **Attribution params on that slug route are fully attacker-controlled and reflected verbatim** — `GET core.hypofriend.de/tools?utm_source=attacker&utm_medium=x&utm_campaign=evil&redirect=evil` → 301 `…/en/exchange?link_id=cb8917e2…&redirect=evil&share_id=dddb5cba…&utm_campaign=evil&utm_medium=x&utm_source=attacker`. With no params the same route emits defaults `utm_source=email&utm_medium=free&utm_campaign=real_estate_v35`. `link_id`/`share_id` stay fixed across all variants → **the link identity is server-bound but its campaign attribution is not bound to it at all.**
[NEW] **Client persistence leg proven in the shipped bundle** (`CMAtwEsq.js`, 200, 1,336,611B): `XP=function(){(query.utm_source||query.utm_medium||query.utm_campaign)&&a2().website.setMarketingCampaign({utm_source:query.utm_source,utm_medium:query.utm_medium,utm_campaign:query.utm_campaign})}` reads utm_* straight off the landing query string and fires the `setMarketingCampaign` GraphQL mutation; the same values are written to sticky first-party storage under fixed keys `hypo_utm_source` / `hypo_utm_medium` / `hypo_utm_campaing` (sic) and `hypofriend_user_web_session_utm_*`.
