- **[PARKED]** "The forged `/en/account` link is a trusted-domain credential-phishing URL": **withdrawn by my own control, not by inspection.** The destination is a 3766B `server: AmazonS3` shell, `x-frame-options: DENY`, with no `__NUXT__` and no reflected campaign value, loading its own bundle rather than the main app. There is no attacker-controlled content at the destination. Prior cycle's phishing framing overstated the finding; the correct reading is an honest first-party URL carrying poisoned attribution.
- **[PARKED]** "`ChatLinkPreviewPost` is an SSRF vector": dropped before it matured. It is `post(slug:$slug, locale:$locale)` — a CMS content lookup keyed by slug, not a URL fetch. Recorded so it cannot later drift into a false SSRF lead.
- **[PARKED]** "`partner_id` in the new bundle is the referral-partner binding": dropped. It is PostHog analytics config (`this.config.partnerId` beside `plan` and `ingestion_metadata`).
