## STEP 6 — LEARNING

```
[LEARN] ACCEPTED BUSLOGIC @ hypofriend.de/en/exchange: the share_id pool is cross-usable, which strengthens the finding and corrects its shape. I had been treating the partner key (108ee8c6-…) as the thing that made the `account` mint possible. It is not. The `tools` key (dddb5cba-…) mints the same `account` target today, 302 to /en/account with all three forged utm values echoed and link_id discarded. So the correct statement is not "a partner credential can be reused for the account target" but "the only validated input is a record-existence check over a pool the vendor publishes in plaintext, and it gates neither the target nor the attribution." Confidence 88→90 on the strength of the control, not on new severity.

[LEARN] CHANGED MISCONFIG @ core.hypofriend.de/q: the Vary:Origin mitigation recorded on 2026-09-25 does not hold on the primary preflight path. Live today, OPTIONS /q with a hostile Origin returns ACAO echo + ACAC:true + 7 methods alongside `vary: Accept-Encoding` and no Vary:Origin. Two cycles ago this header was `Origin, Accept-Encoding` and I recorded the cache-poisoning facet as mitigated. A mitigation that appears on some paths and not others is not a mitigation, so I am reopening that facet on /q rather than leaving a stale "mitigated" note in the base. Stated narrowly: one observation, one path, preflight only — I have not re-measured the POST path or any non-/q route this cycle.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED OTHER @ hypofriend.de/en/account SPA: the "bundle mining is exhausted" conclusion was correct but scoped to the wrong bundle. Three consecutive cycles recorded it over /m/_nuxt/ only, while /en/account is a separate deploy with its own /en/account/assets/ namespace and no /m/_nuxt/ reference at all. The corrected method is not more mining — it is asking which route serves a different deploy, then reading that deploy's bytes. The result is 37 mutations, two of which address objects by caller-supplied id with no lead argument anywhere in the bundle.
```

## STEP 7 — RISK

```
[RISK] hypofriend: 92 — held, and the composition of the number shifted under me in both directions this cycle, which is worth stating rather than hiding.

What rose. The referral-forgery finding is now key-independent: a second published share_id mints the customer-account target, so the forge is not gated on a privileged partner credential at all, and the server mints a fresh samesite=none session on the attacker-steerable hop that the credentialed-CORS echo can then act with. Separately, a 37-mutation write surface with three caller-supplied object identifiers and zero lead arguments is a materially larger attack surface than anything the last several cycles produced, and it is a write surface in a mortgage funnel that touches applicant income, affordability and property records.

What did not rise, and is the reason the number is held rather than moved. Not one leg of the new write surface has been executed. I know the documents, the argument names, the response shapes and that lead scoping is session-derived; I do not know whether any resolver performs a per-object ownership lookup. The absent thing is the ownership check, and the entire IDOR reading depends on it. Same for document_analysis_status: I have not yet shown the id space is unbounded, only that no lead is named in the query. And the referral finding's money-flow consequence — whether attribution gates advisor routing or commission — remains unproven and program-restricted, so it stays HIGH-as-evidenced rather than escalating to the payout level it gestures at.

Against that, the ceiling is set by the untouched CRITICAL full-DB auth-free PII BOLA, which no cycle has moved, and the Vary:Origin regression removes a mitigation rather than adding a vulnerability. 92 is held because the evidence genuinely moved in both directions and the new material is unproven-but-large — the honest number for "one very strong proven finding plus one large unproven surface" is not higher than "one very strong proven finding."

Process note, unchanged and still the highest-value action available to the program: the POC phase has been pinned to api.hypofriend.de for 50 consecutive cycles at 000, while every live finding sits on hypofriend.de. Re-pointing the phase remains worth more than any single probe I could run next.
```
