[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ core.hypofriend.de/q + hypofriend.de/q: introspection is off but the error channel defeats it — `undefinedField` returns the parent `typeName` (`HypofriendType`, `Lead`), answers bulk field-existence in one request, and the did-you-mean suggester returns the real field name (`formAuthenticityToken` → `form_authenticity_token`). This overturns the standing REJECTED "introspection disabled, no schema dump vector". The class boundary I had to argue past is "descriptive errors", and the argument is that a stack trace is incidental whereas this reconstructs the specific artefact the vendor chose to protect, using a graphql-ruby feature that is configuration-off by default — so the remediation is a config line, not a code fix. That is the difference between a banner and a bypass, and it is why I am filing it rather than filing it as evidence.

[LEARN] REJECTED IDOR @ core.hypofriend.de/q (document_analysis_status): my own [NEXT] discriminator returned `{"documentAnalysisStatus":null}` for a well-formed non-existent UUID. The field is live and unauthenticated, but it binds to the id, so arbitrary ids yield nothing and the "existence oracle" framing was wrong — I asserted a read primitive on an inference about argument shape and had not run the one cheap probe that would have settled it. I should have run it two cycles ago instead of ranking it at 58 on structural reasoning. Hypothesis closed at 30, dropped from the survivor list, and the withdrawal is explicit rather than a quiet absence.

[LEARN] CHANGED MISCONFIG @ core.hypofriend.de/q: I recorded on 2026-09-27 13:09Z that the `Vary:Origin` mitigation had "reverted" on the primary preflight path, and generalised it into reopening the cache-poisoning facet. A paired measurement on the same host and path today shows POST /q returns `vary: Accept,Origin,Accept-Encoding` while OPTIONS returns `vary: Accept-Encoding`. The mitigation was never reverted; only the preflight omits the header, and since browser preflight caching is keyed on the (origin, url, method, headers) tuple rather than on a Vary-selected representation, the residual facet is close to inert. I generalised a mitigation's absence from a single path, which is the same error I made in the opposite direction on 2026-09-25. Paired controls on the same endpoint are the cheapest defence I have and I skipped them.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED NG @ hypofriend.de/m/_nuxt/Bitus3YJ.js: 7th entry rename in 9 days, 1,336,611B, sha256 `a28e9773a9fd290f2945b81c2a9a7742ba433eeadeec3e5d29b79b0b66c8a64a`, buildId `0e770bb9-…`. Same byte size as `CMAtwEsq.js` but a different hash, so this is a real content change, not a rename — yet all 10 named-op template counts are bit-identical and no host was added. Fourth consecutive cycle confirming the main bundle is exhausted as a discovery source, and this cycle's entire new surface came from the API's own error output rather than from either bundle. The pivot that keeps paying is not "mine deeper" but "ask the server what it will admit to".

## STEP 7 — RISK

[RISK] hypofriend: 92 — held, and the composition moved again in a direction I want on the record rather than buried. Nothing new exposed customer data this cycle: the one probe that could have touched a customer record returned `null` because the id matched nothing, and the account bundle is bit-stable for the fourth cycle. So the number does not rise. What did change is that the *cost of reaching everything else* fell. Until today, mapping the `/q` schema required mining a 1.3MB public bundle and manually normalising camelCase — which is why three cycles of "op-mining exhausted" produced negative results. The server now supplies type names and correct field names on request, unauthenticated, on both hosts. Every standing hypothesis in this program whose open gate was "find the field name" has had that gate removed, while the gates that remain — bulk PII quantification, ownership of a document id, attribution persistence on a lead — are all HUMAN_ONLY because they require touching customer data. The risk is therefore unchanged in kind and lower in the effort an attacker must spend, which is the profile I would expect to convert into a bounty payout on the first authorised test rather than in the program.
