## STEP 1 — DELTA

- **[NEW]** `root.form_authenticity_token` on `/q` is now **server-confirmed live** — returns an 86-char per-session Rails CSRF token. Prior cycle this was only *inferred* from `/crm`'s inline JS.
- **[NEW]** `/en/plus/q` and `/q` are the **same schema**, not distinct. Both root fields are type `HypofriendType` with the identical 7 fields; identical `Lead`. Corrects a 3-week-old "distinct schema, never mapped" belief.
- **[NEW]** `Lead.documents` → type `Document`, fields `id`, `type`, `file_name` — the read-side identifier that the standing write primitive `deleteLeadDocumentAttachment(input:{id: ID!})` consumes, now mapped server-side with no bundle.
- **[NEW]** Unmapped type edges: `Lead.advisor`/`primary_advisor` → `Advisor`; `Lead.referrer` → `Lead` (self-referential referral chain).
- **[NEW]** `root` is exactly 7 fields. `calculateCityTax` and `jiyuCalculate` are now **gone**, joining `calculateMaklerFee` (removed 2026-09-10). This surface is shrinking.
- **[NEW]** `hypofriend.de/crm` `<form method="post" action="/auth/google_oauth2">` sources its token via `fetch("/q", {query: root { form_authenticity_token }})` — the vendor's own internal backoffice form reads the token from the endpoint now proven cross-origin-readable.
