**[NEW]**

1. **`/api/v3/chatbase` — LLM gateway behind the customer account** (new route, new deploy)
   Today's `/en/account` bundle calls `POST {baseUrl}/api/v3/chatbase` with per-locale agent IDs hardcoded in public JS: `en` `GCVrYdVi90Ge3-p1bf_fK` (sha256 `66940a222bb18ad28d78a63c7f05f01de9f7965d79c71547f2fd796fdd513028`), `de` `JtEAojiaJT5AiQBlRkrQL` (sha256 `45c971875d912c6c1abc437bd703d83f29f58606828c88de1a85d4be32b4565d`). `withCredentials:true`, and `identity:()=>({leadId, givenName})` forwards lead identity to the model. System prompt, turn-hint rules, CTA action list and `segmentOptions` are **100% client-side** — the "Hypofriend Plus is only available in Berlin" business rule is enforced nowhere server-side.
   These IDs are served to every anonymous visitor, so they are client-public identifiers, not credentials. No secret is claimed.

2. **8th bundle rename in 48h on `/en/account`** — `index-DwBItw8U.js` (8 cycles live) → **301**, replaced by `index-BLX7yr-v.js` (2,468,656 B, ETag `"be788be0758c8675f0455c5ececa2260"`, Last-Modified `Tue, 29 Sep 2026 13:58:59 GMT`, SHA-256 `4304a74473862400498e26eb8c366f4447d022aedba90679ea43b846b7fee3d3`). 37 distinct named mutations, 72 template occurrences, same object-addressing inputs.

3. **`/api/v3/advisors` is the only discriminating `/api/v3/` control** — `GET` → `401`, 27 bytes, whereas `/api/v3/chatbase` and `/api/v3/zzz-nonexistent-9f2` are byte-identical (`301`, 0 bytes). This is what lets me *not* over-claim.

