reasoning: Introspection is disabled, but the coercion channel leaks more than the field-existence oracle already filed on 2026-09-27. `mutation { selectOffer(input:{}) { __typename } }` returns `Argument 'offerProductId' on InputObject 'SelectOfferInput' is required. Expected type ID!` with a machine-readable `extensions` block. This recovered four input-object type names, their required attribute names and their exact GraphQL types — `SelectOfferInput`, `PropertyMutationsUpdateInput`, `RequestOfferRenewalInput`, `DeleteLeadDocumentAttachmentInput` — with zero data returned and no resolver invoked, because coercion precedes resolution. Combined with the previously filed `undefinedField` type-name leak and the did-you-mean suggester, the same channel reconstructs both halves of the schema the vendor chose to protect.
