[HYP] Presigned-upload chain lets a caller bind an arbitrary S3 object key to a lead document, with no ownership argument on the write
class: BUSLOGIC
asset: core.hypofriend.de/q + hypofriend.de/en/account/assets/index-BLX7yr-v.js
confidence: 64
reasoning: All three legs are now read directly out of the shipped bundle. `createUploadUrl(input:{fileName, contentType})` returns `{s3Key, presignedUrl}`; the client then does a direct credential-free `PUT` to that URL and finally calls `uploadDocumentExtended(input:{type, file_name, file_type, file_link, document_type, applicant_type})` where `file_link` is the S3 key and `JSON.stringify` is applied to `fileName` but **not** to `file_link` or `contentType`. Neither the query `lead { documents { document_attachments { id } } }` nor any mutation input in the bundle carries a `leadId`, so object selection is by opaque identifier alone. `deleteLeadDocumentAttachment(input:{id})` is the same shape and is destructive. `selectOffer`/`requestOfferRenewal` take `offerProductId` and `setOfferViewedByCustomerAt` takes `offerId`, and `offerId` is confirmed client-visible as response data. All five documented coercion-satisfying mutations returned `301 → https://hypofriend.de/` with empty bodies and no 401/403 anywhere, so the only observed gate is a redirect, not an authorization decision.
evidence_needed: an authenticated call with an owned `file_link`/`id` returning `200`, and the same mutation with a foreign identifier returning an authorization error rather than a 301; or any 401/403 on the mutation surface; or a non-redirect error body naming the record.
verify_steps: 1) `GET https://core.hypofriend.de/q` to establish a jar; 2) re-send the *validation-failing* document `{"query":"mutation { createUploadUrl(input:{}) { presignedUrl } }"}` twice — once with no Cookie, once with the jar — and diff status, `Location` and the `extensions` block. A coercion error in both runs proves the gate sits strictly after coercion and is therefore the only thing standing between an unauthenticated caller and the resolver; any difference between the two runs proves the gate is session-dependent. This document invokes no resolver because coercion precedes resolution.
impact: if authorization is absent, an authenticated customer could bind or delete another lead's mortgage documents and select offer products by identifier on a lending platform — document destruction plus money-adjacent state change, high severity. Nil if the 301 is a hard login gate.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

