STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

[PARKED] `/api/v3/chatbase` as an unauthenticated third-party LLM proxy: killed by control, not by inspection. `GET` returns `301 → https://hypofriend.de/` on **both** origin and edge, identical to every unknown path in the canonical redirect shell, so the vendor's server-side Chatbase credential is not reachable on this deploy. The route reference, the two workspace IDs and the shipped system prompt stay on record as assets should the route appear on a future deploy — but the hypothesis itself is closed at 0 and is not carried.
[PARKED] Raw `${}` interpolation of `contentType` and `file_link` into query text as a GraphQL document-injection primitive: dropped. The interpolation happens in the vendor's own client and the interpolated values originate from server responses, so an attacker who controls them only rewrites their own document — and the server-side gate applies to the whole document regardless. This is a hygiene note inside hypothesis 1, not a finding of its own.
