## STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE

Dropping the object-addressing IDOR. My discriminator was designed as "200 JSON error vs GraphQL not-found vs 301 vs 401/403", and the measured 301-to-canonical-shell with an empty body swallows every authz signal — **the test is structurally incapable of answering whether authorization exists behind it**. This is the third time I have asserted a shape from argument structure without a working discriminator (`document_analysis_status` 09-27, `exposeSeen` 09-29, `unclaimLead` 09-25). Confidence 55 → 32, below the drop threshold, and the withdrawal is explicit.

I also had to discard two of my own controls this cycle: `requestAccountLink(input:{})` did not satisfy (`email: EmailAddress!` required) and `setLocale(locale:)` did not exist (`setLocale` takes `input`). Neither licenses any conclusion. The asymmetry question — **is the 301 gate keyed on caller-supplied object identifiers, or applied to every satisfying mutation?** — is therefore *unanswered*, not answered. I could not build a satisfying mutation with no identifier and no side effect, so I am recording it as blocked rather than guessing.

```
[PARKED] Object-addressing mutations accept caller-supplied IDs with no lead/tenant argument — discriminator invalid: 301-to-canonical-shell with empty body returns no authz signal and no 401/403 exists on the write surface, so status-code cannot separate "authz behind redirect" from "no authz". Re-posable only in the query direction, where the surface is ungated.
[PARKED] SSRF-to-cloud-metadata — 37 mutations re-mined across the /en/account bundle; zero URL/uri/endpoint/webhook/proxy-accepting GraphQL argument. Closed against the largest deploy.
[PARKED] /en/exchange share-link forge — arbitrary link_id minted, share_id auth-by-obscurity, utm_* raw pass-through, redirect allowlist {expose,account}. Mature; destination proven to be a byte-identical 3766B static shell, so impact is a credible first-party URL plus poisoned attribution, not a data read.
[PARKED] Enum-value recovery via invalid-enum error — closed this cycle: argumentLiteralsIncompatible returns the type name and argument but enumerates no members.
[PARKED] /en/exchange "record not found" oracle — rejected earlier: it always returns "not found", no discriminator.
[FINAL] 1. MISCONFIG core.hypofriend.de/q — error channel as unauthenticated cross-origin write-surface contract oracle — 88 — PASSIVE
[FINAL] 2. MISCONFIG core.hypofriend.de/property-search-api — native unauthenticated full-schema dump, cross-referenceable against the /q map — 71 — PASSIVE
[FINAL] 3. AUTH core.hypofriend.de/api/v3/advisors — sole authenticated endpoint's credential in the public bundle on a credentialed-CORS route — 76 — HUMAN_ONLY
```

