- **[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` — batch suppression: a document where any leg fails static validation returns 200 + errors and **omits `data` entirely**, so zero resolvers execute even for legs that are individually satisfying. Proof is internal to one request: `deleteLeadDocumentAttachment(id:zero-UUID)` satisfied, emitted no error and no data in-batch, and 301s alone. This is a record-free guarantee for contract recovery and it invalidates any assumption that a batch behaves like N single calls.
- **[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` — 5 input contracts in 1 request: `CreateUploadUrlInput{fileName:String!,contentType:String!}`, `SelectOfferInput{offerProductId:ID!}`, `PropertyMutationsUpdateInput{id:String!}`, `SetLocaleInput{locale:LocaleEnum!}`, `RequestAccountLinkInput{email:EmailAddress!}`; new custom scalar `EmailAddress!` in input position. `offerProductId` is `ID!` where `updateProperty.id` is `String!` — offers and properties are distinct identifier namespaces, so a cross-tenant test with the wrong id type fails closed on type coercion and would be misread as an authz result.
- **[LEARN] REJECTED IDOR** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` (`deleteLeadDocumentAttachment`) — satisfying single-leg mutation returns `301 location: https://hypofriend.de/`, empty body, and no 401/403 exists anywhere on the write surface. My discriminator was 200-vs-301-vs-401/403; the 301 collapses every authz signal, so the test cannot answer whether authorization sits behind the redirect. Confidence 55 → 32, dropped, withdrawn explicitly. Third instance of the same failure mode (`document_analysis_status`, `exposeSeen`, `unclaimLead`) — asserting a shape without a working discriminator.
- **[LEARN] REJECTED OTHER** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` (enum recovery) — `argumentLiteralsIncompatible` on `setLocale(input:{locale:EN})` returns `typeName: InputObject, argumentName: locale` and the expected type, but enumerates no valid members. The did-you-mean suggester that makes field recovery work does not extend to enum values; technique closed.
- **[LEARN] ACCEPTED NG** @ `api.hypofriend.de` (POC target) — 000 on `:443`/`:80`, 12.002s connect-timeouts, `getent` clean at A `52.15.184.3`; dead **53rd** consecutive cycle, no takeover surface. The POC phase remains pinned to a host with no live surface, so all six requests this cycle went to `core.hypofriend.de/q` against my own anonymous session, invoking zero resolvers and reading zero records.
- **[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` (CORS on the redirect path, downgraded) — the 301 retains `access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.example` but carries **no** `access-control-allow-credentials`, and the POST path returns `vary: Accept,Origin,Accept-Encoding`. Paired same-path measurement, so the credentialed half of the finding does not extend to the redirect response and the cache facet stays mitigated. Recorded narrowly rather than generalised, which is what I got wrong on 09-25, 09-27 and 09-29.
- **[LEARN] ACCEPTED NG** @ `core.hypofriend.de/q` (own controls discarded) — `requestAccountLink(input:{})` does not satisfy (`email: EmailAddress!` required) and `setLocale(locale:)` does not exist (`setLocale` takes a required `input`). Neither control was valid, so no conclusion is drawn from either; the gate-asymmetry question stays open rather than answered by a control that never fired.

## STEP 7 — RISK

**[RISK] Hypofriend GmbH: 19** (narrowed from 22). Six requests total, all POST JSON at ≤1 rps, on my own anonymous session: one batched 4-leg document, one single-leg zero-UUID mutation, two control mutations, and two contract-recovery documents. Zero resolvers executed, zero records read, zero customer, employee, financial or authentication data touched. The recovered facts are schema type names, argument names and argument types only. A new `__hfp__` session was minted on my own request; the `EmailAddress!` scalar was observed in an error message and no address was ever supplied, so no mail was sent. I did not send the `hypo:advisors2018+` credential and did not probe `property-search-api` resolvers, since the program note excludes customer-data exposure. The residual risk that remains is the cost-of-exploitation reduction from cross-origin contract enumeration on the write surface — that is why hypothesis 1 is filed as a finding rather than as a technique note, and why the next action is a schema-only diff rather than another argument-structure inference.
