+Every triager cycle also runs the **hygiene gate** (`scripts/hygiene.py`), after the model writes
+and before the commit step:
+
+- `hygiene.py scrub` redacts customer PII *values* from `triage/`, `reports/`, `leads/`,
+  `knowledge/`, `inventory/` and `analyst-out.txt`. Schema field names (`phoneNumber`,
+  `ownerCompany`, ...) are documentation and are deliberately kept; only values are removed.
+  High-entropy ids become salted `<sha256:…>` tokens so the loop can still tell "same record seen
+  again" from "new record" after redaction. Phone numbers are masked, never hashed — ~10^11 is
+  brute-forceable. Known limitation: a bare 8-hex id fragment with no elision marker survives.
+- `hygiene.py ledger` recomputes `reports/valid-bugs.md` instead of trusting a hand-maintained
+  number, and flags verdicts that hit the program's always-rejected list, verdicts with no finding
+  recorded, HOLDs counted as VALID, and the same finding scored differently across runs.
+- `scripts/test_hygiene.py` covers the scrubber's false positives (CI addresses, Sentry DSNs,
+  GraphQL enum arguments, git SHAs, CVSS scores, timestamps).
+
 Testing discipline: rate-limited (1 rps), no DoS/account-lockout, writes only on non-prod/test
 assets, no exposure of customer/employee/financial/auth data, secrets committed only as hashes.
 
+> The discipline line above is enforced by the hygiene gate, not merely intended. It was
+> previously only prose: live customer phone numbers, owner names/companies and expose UUIDs
+> were being re-quoted into committed artifacts every cycle, which `scope.yml` excludes as
+> "exposure of customer/employee/financial/authentication data during testing".
+
 > IMPORTANT: the pipeline produces CANDIDATE leads. A reportable, validated finding requires
 > human triage + proof against the program's gate. No finding is fabricated; scanner output alone
 > is never accepted. Active testing is gated behind the in-scope hosts in `inventory/hypofriend.md` and
 > must stay within the program's published scope.
