**Server:** `https://hypofriend.de` · `https://core.hypofriend.de`
**Phase:** POC · **Target:** `api.hypofriend.de` (DNS-resolved `52.15.184.3`, no live surface this cycle)
**Cycle date:** 2026-10-02 · **Mode:** passive-first, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS + record-free poisoned GraphQL documents only

[CHANGED] `/content/q/` on **hypofriend.de** and **core.hypofriend.de** is a **live fourth GraphQL instance**. The knowledge base records `POST /content/q → 404`; that 404 was a **GET artifact**. A POST returns a valid graphql-ruby envelope (`{"meta":{"status":0,"key":"OK"}}`, HTTP 200, `application/json`). Both hosts byte-identical (1238 B for the same document).

[CHANGED] Resolved the `/en/account` transport mystery. `acct.js` `postGraphQL` (sha256 `4304a74473862400498e26eb8c366f4447d022aedba90679ea43b846b7fee3d3`, bit-stable since 2026-09-30) resolves its base as `window.location.protocol + "//" + window.location.hostname + (isContent ? "/content" : "")`, then posts to `` `${r}/q/` `` — **current origin, trailing slash**, with `isContent` selecting `/content/q/`. The 37 mutations therefore hit `/q/` on whichever host serves the page, not `coreApiUrl`. Earlier `serverUrl` (18 hits) is Amplitude telemetry and irrelevant.

[CHANGED] `/content/q/` has **no write surface**: `POST` of any mutation returns `{"code":"missingMutationConfiguration"}` — *"Schema is not configured for mutations"*. This is a config-level negative control, not an authorization outcome, so it is stronger than the 301 write-gate evidence used elsewhere. Introspection is also disabled (`__schema` → `undefinedField` on `Query`).

[CHANGED] Credentialed CORS is live on `/content/q/` at both hosts: `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` reflects `https://evil.example`, `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`, `Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS, HEAD`, `Max-Age: 7200`. `X-Frame-Options` differs per host: edge `DENY`, origin `SAMEORIGIN`, `/q` `ALLOWALL`.

[PRIO] ~~Confirm the mutation endpoint used by the `/en/account` deploy~~ — **resolved** above; endpoint is origin-relative `${hostname}/q/`.

[PRIO] ~~Determine whether `/content/q/` is reachable by the shipped client~~ — **resolved**; it is the content-mode target.

[PRIO] ~~Resolve `/content/q/` query surface~~ — **partially resolved**: 45 distinct candidate field names probed (18 + 27 batches, all via a poison field guaranteeing zero resolvers, `data` key absent in every response) are **all absent**. Surface is fully disjoint from `/q` — including every field known from `rates_table`, `lead`, `form_authenticity_token`, `property_search`. Not guessable from common CMS naming.

[HYP] **Stale client feature points at a slug-addressed, ungated read primitive.** — The bundle ships `query ChatLinkPreviewPost($slug: String!, $locale: String!) { post(slug:, locale:) { title preview seo_description } }`, invoked with the content flag `!0`, so it targets `/content/q/`. It addresses a CMS post by a **caller-supplied slug with no tenant or owner argument**, and unlike the mutations it is a *query*, so it is not gated by the 301 write-gate. **But the deployed content schema rejects it:** `post` → `undefinedField` on `Query`, on both edge and origin, byte-identically. The bundle wraps the call in `catch{return null}`, so the chat link-preview is **silently dead in the current deploy**. *Impact:* none demonstrable today. *Confidence:* medium-high that the primitive is real and currently unreachable; low that it is exploitable as shipped. Chosen over "empty CMS schema" because a live endpoint whose only client is dead code more likely indicates an undeployed/route-mismatched content backend than an intentionally empty one.

[HYP] **The 404 in the knowledge base was a method artifact, not an absence of route.** — `/content/q` was only ever probed with GET; the POST route exists and is unmapped. *Impact:* every recorded GraphQL 404 in the base may be a false negative, and conversely every "not a GraphQL endpoint" GET conclusion for a Rails path is unverified. *Confidence:* high for `/content/q` (directly demonstrated); unquantified elsewhere. Chosen because it invalidates a whole class of recorded negatives rather than adding one.

[PARKED] ~~Chat link-preview route leak / SSRF~~ — reopened and closed in this cycle: schema field absent, zero exploitability. Will not revisit unless the content schema is restored.

[PARKED] ~~Routing bypass via GraphQL path variants~~ — closed with a control. `POST /q/` and `POST /q` return **byte-identical bodies** after masking `serverTime` (both sha256 `fc61e959138ef45812929efdf6c6df51e46d9433211362dc51880fdc05310d24`). Trailing slash is the same route; not a bypass. Consistent with the prior trailing-slash-on-slug-routes finding.

[PARKED] ~~Object addressing in the 37 `/en/account` mutations~~ — `missingMutationConfiguration` on the content schema and the 301 write-gate on `/q` keep all four candidates (`selectOffer.offerProductId`, `updateProperty.id`, `deleteLeadDocumentAttachment.id`, `requestOfferRenewal.offerProductId`) parked for per-resolver authorization testing.

[FINAL] No critical, high, medium, or low vulnerability is proven this cycle. All findings are negative controls, a dead-code observation, or a knowledge-base correction. Nothing meets the reporting bar.

