## Objective
- Conduct deep-hunt bug bounty analysis against Hypofriend GmbH in-scope assets (mortgage platform, APIs, portals, web/apps, domains).
- Identify real logic flaws (IDOR/BOLA, auth/session, SSRF-to-cloud-metadata, mass assignment, GraphQL, OAuth, business logic) while adhering to strict read-only/passive constraints.

## Important Details
- **Program scope**: All Hypofriend GmbH and affiliated brands company-owned infrastructure, platforms, customer portals, APIs, mobile/web apps, websites, domains.
- **Constraints**: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only when probing live; <=1 rps; no auth-bypass or mutating tests against live customer data; no endpoint-map-only claims; sha256 any secret; facts vs hypotheses strictly separated.
- **Out of scope (REJECTED)**: DoS/rate-limit/lockout, descriptive headers/errors only, robots.txt, self-XSS, username enumeration policy, TLS best practice, clickjacking without exploit, mail/SPF/DKIM/DMARC, logout-CSRF, scanner-only.
- **Top confirmed issue**: `core.hypofriend.de/property-search-api` — unauthenticated full-DB BOLA via `propertySearch→exposes→expose` returning broker/owner PII (cellPhoneNumber, phoneNumber, propertyOwnerLastName, providerEmail, ownerCompany, providerCompany); direct origin bypasses CloudFront WAF. (Confidence 92, CRITICAL)
- **Key chain findings**: Global credentialed CORS on Rails origin (echoes any Origin + `access-control-allow-credentials:true` + 7 methods) across `/q`, `/content/q/`, `/en/plus/q`, `/en/health/q`, arbitrary paths; `root.form_authenticity_token` and `root.lead.has_admin_cookie` (JSON scalar, no per-field authz) exposed via `/q` family; introspection bypass via GraphQL error channel (`undefinedField` returns parent `typeName` + did-you-mean suggester).
- **Other active surfaces**: `/en/exchange` — 6-key `share_id` pool, arbitrary `link_id` mintable, `utm_*` raw pass-through into 302 Location (attribution unbound); 4 object-addressing mutations in `/en/account` deploy (`selectOffer:offerProductId`, `updateProperty:id`, `deleteLeadDocumentAttachment:id`, `requestOfferRenewal:offerProductId`) with no lead/tenant arg; `core.hypofriend.de/api/v3/advisors` uses hardcoded HTTP Basic `hypo:advisors2018+` (`Basic aHlwbzphZHZpc29yczIwMTgr`, b64 sha256 `56f00b87...`) shipped in public bundle; `/content/q/` is live fourth GraphQL instance (POST 200, credentialed CORS, mutations disabled via `missingMutationConfiguration`).
- **Fleet state**: `api.hypofriend.de` (POC target) is **dead 54th consecutive cycle** (000 on :443/:80, A `52.15.184.3`, 12s timeouts) — phase mismatch (pinned to dead host). `*.app.hypofriend.de` (uploader/frontend/appointments/profile/admin) all resolve to single A `52.14.251.223` (TCP-filtered on :80/:443) — EIP-recycling takeover window (cloud-side decisive). `mobile.hypofriend.de` on own ELB triple with zero healthy targets (503 awselb/2.0). `images/assets/static/maps` 503 on shared ELB. `sparplan.hypofriend.de` + `heyflow.hypofriend.de` CNAME to `flow.heyflow.domains` with TLS `sslv3 alert handshake failure` (delegated to Cloudflare/heyflow) — REJECTED as attacker-controllable.
- **Inventory stable**: 71 hosts discovered; main live web surface centered on `hypofriend.de` and `core.hypofriend.de` (direct Rails origin). Entry bundles renamed frequently (`D9p-7uJV.js→g8upYJar.js→B9bmTtuA.js→CYL-uMFM.js→CqlAYNcX.js→CQoy7ifk.js→DRDuhMz8.js→CMAtwEsq.js→Bitus3YJ.js`) — bundle mining exhausted as discovery source (path breadth + error channel + public asset mining now primary).

## Work State

### Completed
- **Fleet mapping**: Identified live/dead hosts, direct-origin vs CloudFront edge, ELB fingerprints, ngrok dead (`*.local.hypofriend.de` ERR_NGROK_3200, folded into 503 fleet).
- **Property-search-api validation**: Full-DB BOLA chain `propertySearch→exposes→expose` re-confirmed live returning PII; direct-origin bare headers vs edge CF stack; introspection enabled; crawl primitives (`pagination/exposes/exposesInBounds/mapExposes`, `expose(id,leadId,saveExposeContact,returnMissing)`); write primitives `favoriteExpose`, `informationRequest` (stack-trace disclosure) documented.
- **/q family mapping**: All instances (`/q`, `/en/plus/q`, `/en/health/q`, `/content/q/`) mapped; credentialed CORS global; introspection bypass via error channel; `root.form_authenticity_token`, `root.lead.has_admin_cookie`, `rates_table`, `appointment_availability`, `uploadDocumentExtended`, `processLeadForAppointment`, etc.; `calculateMaklerFee` removed from `/q` HypofriendType schema between cycles.
- **/en/account deploy mined**: `index-BLX7yr-v.js` (2,468,656B, 37 mutations) exposes 4 object-addressing mutations with caller-supplied IDs and `sendVerifiedListingEmail`, `submitDocumentAnalysis(files: JSON blob)`; `createUploadUrl` returns `{s3Key,presignedUrl}`; `file_link` is caller-supplied S3 key in `uploadDocumentExtended`.
- **/en/exchange**: 6-key `share_id` pool cross-usable, arbitrary `link_id` mintable, `utm_*` raw pass-through, `redirect` allowlist `{expose,account}` only (other values 404), fresh anonymous session minted per request; destination shell byte-identical between forged/real IDs.
- **/crm + /api/v3**: `/crm` internal backoffice login page (edge-only S3+Lambda); `/api/v3/advisors` 401 Basic with hardcoded credential shipped in bundle; `/api/v3/delete-cookie` and `/api/v3/delete-admin-cookie` 200 unauth (logout-CSRF class, retained only for context); `/api/v3/chatbase` route discovered (301 on origin+edge).
- **Error/response classes**: `GET /404` and `/500` return HTTP 200 with static Nuxt error documents; global rack-cors confirmed on arbitrary paths; origin `XFO:ALLOWALL` vs edge `XFO:DENY` persistent on many routes.

### Active
- **Top hypothesis #1 (IDOR/BOLA)**: `core.hypofriend.de/property-search-api` full-DB auth-free PII read via `propertySearch→exposes→expose` — confidence 92, CRITICAL. Only open gate is HUMAN bulk quantification (program-excludes customer data retrieval). Direct-origin WAF bypass confirmed.
- **Top hypothesis #2 (MISCONFIG/AUTH chain)**: `/q` family cross-origin CSRF-token + session-identity read via global credentialed CORS + `SameSite=None` cookies (`root.form_authenticity_token`, `root.lead.has_admin_cookie`) — confidence 55, MEDIUM (state-changing leg unproven). Introspection bypass via error channel live.
- **Top hypothesis #3 (OTHER/Takeover window)**: `*.app.hypofriend.de` stale A `52.14.251.223` (TCP-filtered) — EIP-recycling takeover window; confidence 45, INFORMATIONAL (cloud-side decisive). `mobile.hypofriend.de` ELB zero-target noted but no security impact.

### Blocked
- **POC phase mismatch**: `api.hypofriend.de` designated target is dead 54th consecutive cycle (000 :443/:80) — no live surface for phase completion; all activity constrained to read-only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS <=1 rps.
- **Program data exclusion**: Bulk quantification of `property-search-api` PII or executing mutating tests against live customer data is not permitted (HUMAN_ONLY with explicit written authorization). 
- **Cloud-side checks required**: EIP allocation status of `52.14.251.223` (app tier) and AWS ELB target health ownership cannot be determined remotely.
- **State-changing leg unproven**: Cross-origin CSRF-token exploitation against `/q` family requires authenticated victim + POST mutation — outside current read-only constraints.

## Next Move
1. **Immediate (PASSIVE/READ-ONLY)**: Re-verify `/q` family CORS preflight/POST `Vary` asymmetry and confirm `root.form_authenticity_token` + `root.lead.has_admin_cookie` exposure on `hypofriend.de/q`, `core.hypofriend.de/q`, `/en/plus/q`, `/en/health/q`, `/content/q/` with single OPTIONS/POST `{__typename}` or minimal read-only queries (no customer data). 
2. **Next (HUMAN/PROGRAM GATE)**: Escalate property-search-api bulk enumeration and `informationRequest` write-path testing to program for explicit written authorization (HUMAN_ONLY). In parallel request cloud-side confirmation of `52.14.251.223` EIP allocation and `mobile.hypofriend.de` ELB target state.

