## [OBJECTIVE]
Re-verify the Hypofriend senior analyst surface against the current live state, re-rank assets, update hypotheses, and select exactly one passive-first next action. Scope: Hypofriend-owned infrastructure and applications only.

## [DELTA]
**D1 — Mobile ELB tier is now partially LIVE (new).** `63.176.45.32` and `63.182.230.5` now present valid TLS: `CN = hypofriend.de`, `issuer = Amazon RSA 2048 M01`. Both answer `HTTP/2 503`, `server: awselb/2.0`, empty target group. Previously recorded as dead/availability-only. `63.189.130.21` remains fully closed. **Classification refined, not escalated** — ELB listeners are up but no healthy backends; still availability-only, not reportable.

**D2 — `/property-search-api` re-characterized as POST-only GraphQL with stripped introspection.** A `GET` returns `this endpoint exclusively POST requests`. The body contract is `{"query":"…"}`. `__schema` is absent (`undefinedField`), but the field-level error channel still leaks names, required args, and existence signals. `propertySearch` no longer exists under that name; the live fields are `exposes(id)` and `expose(id)`.

**D3 — `expose`/`exposes` differential existence oracle (new, incremental).** Both accept a single `id` with **no auth argument and no auth gate** (unauthenticated calls return HTTP 200). `expose(id)` returns `not found: \`<id>\`` for absent ids; `exposes(id)` returns `[]`. The two fields disagree on the absent-id case, giving a distinguishable existence signal.

**D4 — No new hostnames anywhere.** Passive reverse-IP on `52.14.251.223` returned only the 5 already-known app names plus `ec2-52-14-251-223.us-east-2.compute.amazonaws.com`. Reverse-IP on `63.176.45.32` returned only its own PTR. `crt.sh` did not respond.

**D5 — Target unchanged.** `api.hypofriend.de` → `52.15.184.3`, `000` connect-timeout on both :80 and :443. **55th consecutive dead cycle.**

